# Feature-first

One feature folder holds every layer. Opening it shows the whole use case. The composition root and a small shared kernel stay outside.

## Serverpod

```
lib/src/features/notes/domain/
lib/src/features/notes/application/
lib/src/features/notes/infra/
lib/src/features/notes/presentation/     endpoint and its wire mapper
lib/src/shared/
lib/src/app/
```

The wire mapper sits next to that feature's endpoint. Do not add a shared `presentation/mappers/` file.

## Flutter

```
lib/features/notes/domain/
lib/features/notes/application/
lib/features/notes/data/
lib/features/notes/presentation/     page, notifier, and tile
lib/shared/
lib/app/providers.dart
lib/app/router/
```

The shell router lives in `app/router/` so it is not trapped inside one feature. The tile sits beside the page and does not import Riverpod.

## Rules

- A feature does not import a sibling feature. A type both need moves to `shared/`.
- `app/` is the only file outside the feature that constructs `*RepositoryImpl`.
- Presentation inside the feature imports the composition root for use cases. It does not import that feature's data or infra implementation.
- A workflow that needs two features' entities does not reach across. Move the shared type out, or the dependency rule is broken.
